{:edb/db-before-t 2304 :edb/db-after-t 2305 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535617 50 #inst "2026-10-09T03:42:47.131Z" 13194139535617 true] [17592186179669 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357704 13194139535617 true] [17592186179669 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357711 13194139535617 true] [17592186179672 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357718 13194139535617 true] [17592186179672 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357725 13194139535617 true] [17592186179951 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535617 true] [17592186179951 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068563/assets/501a3512fb4b8a1898c6dfb8816d587de4a0cd585991d9c92d2bb35d83a2853d.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)$ shown above. Let $C$ be the path where the semicircle is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" 13194139535617 true] [17592186179951 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3694/Source/Images/q-125381.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x, y)$ shown above. Let $C$ be the path where the semicircle is traversed from $A$ to $B$. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $∫_{C}F \\cdot dr > 0$\n2. $∫_{C}F \\cdot dr < 0$\n3. $∫_{-C}F \\cdot dr > 0$" 13194139535617 false] [17592186179951 1145 "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false while statement II is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068563/assets/4c11b38f9e598e0cd8fc50715d2091e5bea48d188440ae8a99c84d66a6acb6b9.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068563/assets/346007ae582fccdf4519a3d1cd50a467e19d5345238343a1311fd3348bbeb138.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139535617 true] [17592186357704 1017 #edb/ref 17592186357705 13194139535617 true] [17592186357704 1089 "q-125491" 13194139535617 true] [17592186357704 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535617 true] [17592186357704 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068563/assets/f0daaf51b1aab267c11b8457b0e7e1480ff5aabd3acaa15a07f54625c6d8103d.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above, and let $C$ be the path where the curve is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$" 13194139535617 true] [17592186357704 1113 #uuid "8ebed4f5-9fd9-56fc-8460-2e87f3659f0d" 13194139535617 true] [17592186357704 1145 "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$  works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068563/assets/1764bfc51a25475162a70bad7239a36f5d099aa6157c71ed7ed3e02e474eb906.png)\n\n \n\nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. It's clear from the picture below that if we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068563/assets/059731f0cac61f19382172192c6a9f7f366ecb758767797f9bc8311faa3865af.png)\n\n \n\nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139535617 true] [17592186357705 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357706 13194139535617 true] [17592186357705 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357707 13194139535617 true] [17592186357705 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357708 13194139535617 true] [17592186357705 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357709 13194139535617 true] [17592186357705 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357710 13194139535617 true] [17592186357705 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535617 true] [17592186357705 1041 "selection" 13194139535617 true] [17592186357705 1104 #edb/ref 17592186357706 13194139535617 true] [17592186357705 1110 #uuid "9f32facd-955d-55fe-886d-ff13a06d7e3c" 13194139535617 true] [17592186357706 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535617 true] [17592186357706 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535617 true] [17592186357706 1111 #uuid "fecaee1b-4337-5bcc-aecf-694c4334311e" 13194139535617 true] [17592186357707 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535617 true] [17592186357707 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535617 true] [17592186357707 1111 #uuid "35f5c612-f14f-57a8-949a-9183101aec8b" 13194139535617 true] [17592186357708 1034